menu "FTM failure investigation"
config FTM_FAILURE_PROBE
    bool "Capture rejected reports inside the audited C6 Wi-Fi blob"
    default n
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6
    help
        Diagnostic only. Exposes three private data symbols in a build-local
        copy of an exact hash-checked blob object. Copies reports before
        driver cleanup, then formats them in a separate task.
config FTM_FAILURE_RETAIN
    bool "Retain discarded quartets and vendor IEs for clock experiments"
    default n
    depends on FTM_FAILURE_PROBE
    help
        Exact-blob diagnostic only. Copies records before cleanup without
        changing timestamps or driver classification. Suppresses verbose
        report logging. Not a portable replacement for a vendor API fix.
config FTM_FAILURE_RX_METADATA
    bool "Capture raw RX descriptor timing fields"
    default n
    depends on FTM_FAILURE_PROBE
    help
        Diagnostic only, gated by the audited wdev and hal_mac object hashes.
        Copies timing fields after the existing hardware timestamp read.
        Adds bounded copying and a short lock to the receive path.
config FTM_FAILURE_ASSOC_TEST
    bool "Disconnect during the fifth FTM session"
    default n
    depends on FTM_FAILURE_PROBE
    help
        Diagnostic only. Disconnect 50 ms after the fifth accepted session
        start to exercise late-report rejection and reassociation recovery.
        Repeats after reboot; restore a build with this option disabled.
config FTM_FAILURE_RESET_TEST
    bool "Run one reconnect and one radio restart after baseline capture"
    default n
    depends on FTM_FAILURE_PROBE
    help
        Diagnostic only. At 60 seconds after the first report, disconnect
        and let the application reconnect. At 120 seconds stop/start Wi-Fi.
        Log completion at 180 seconds. Repeats after each endpoint reboot.
endmenu
